WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Trace the installed measurement

2
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.085
chain from sensing element to displayed
value.

3
00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:09.067
Record the relevant identifiers,
locations, ranges

4
00:00:09.187 --> 00:00:12.237
and configuration against the approved
schedule.

5
00:00:12.357 --> 00:00:15.579
A display tag does not prove which sensor
feeds it.

6
00:00:15.699 --> 00:00:19.048
Installation evidence provides the
configuration

7
00:00:19.168 --> 00:00:22.432
baseline for later assembled-loop checks;
it does

8
00:00:22.552 --> 00:00:26.371
not by itself establish accuracy
throughout operation.

9
00:00:26.991 --> 00:00:31.023
A calibration sticker is a starting point
for locating the record.

10
00:00:31.143 --> 00:00:34.940
Review whether the certificate identifies
the correct instrument

11
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.513
and whether its range, points, method,

12
00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:40.407
results and status support the intended
check.

13
00:00:40.527 --> 00:00:44.772
Consider uncertainty and the applicable
decision rule where relevant.

14
00:00:44.892 --> 00:00:48.177
A current date on an unrelated instrument
certificate

15
00:00:48.297 --> 00:00:51.348
cannot justify using the installed device.

16
00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:54.443
For this fictional arithmetic exercise,

17
00:00:54.563 --> 00:00:57.528
the reference is forty point zero degrees
Celsius

18
00:00:57.648 --> 00:01:00.080
and the indication is forty point four.

19
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.424
Indication minus reference gives plus zero
point four degrees.

20
00:01:04.544 --> 00:01:08.085
With a teaching limit of plus or minus
0.5,

21
00:01:08.205 --> 00:01:10.808
the magnitude is within that simple limit.

22
00:01:10.928 --> 00:01:14.107
This is not a full calibration acceptance
decision;

23
00:01:14.227 --> 00:01:18.152
uncertainty, method and the approved
decision rule still matter.

24
00:01:18.772 --> 00:01:22.825
If an instrument is outside its required
calibration status,

25
00:01:22.945 --> 00:01:26.679
identify which checks relied on it and
assess their validity.

26
00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:29.103
Do not simply obtain a new certificate

27
00:01:29.223 --> 00:01:31.676
and assume earlier readings remain valid.

28
00:01:31.796 --> 00:01:35.167
The investigation may require additional
evidence

29
00:01:35.287 --> 00:01:38.081
or repeated checks under an approved
approach.

30
00:01:38.201 --> 00:01:40.201
Record the basis for the decision

31
00:01:40.321 --> 00:01:42.796
and retain the original observations.
